{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/892450-3e-sidereal-simple-astrology-a-simple-yet-powerful-way-to-cast-your-fate","id":892450,"title":"3e Sidereal SIMPLE Astrology - A simple yet powerful way to cast your fate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-17T06:19:07-07:00","id":892450,"title":"3e Sidereal SIMPLE Astrology - A simple yet powerful way to cast your fate","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A (work in progress) 3e Update to Simple Astrology.</span></span></b><br /> <br /> Sources &amp; Inspiration:<br /> - Manual of Exalted Power 2nd Edition: The Sidereal Exalted<br /> - Shards of the Exalted Dream's Simple Astrology<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidereal Astrology</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Astral Colleges</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The special astral colleges represent a Viziers training in Sidereal astrology, corresponding to the desires and specialties of the various spiders that maintain the Loom of Fate. These are branched into five major categories correlating to the Maidens and the major Constellations in Creation\u2019s sky. Each constellation within rules over a broad, but fluid archetype. One destiny may fall under many constellations.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each of the five colleges is rated from 1 to 5 dots. During character creation: </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">a sidereal begins with one dot in each college; </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">if a sidereal posses a 3 or higher in any of a college's Auspicious abilities, they gain an additional dot toward that college; </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">finally, they gain one additional dot in the college associated with their caste. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Additional dots may be purchased for 2 bonus points or 5 experience points.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The House of Journeys</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Captain </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">leads with strength, determination and order; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Gull</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> wanders without regard for profit; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Mast</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is raw physical exertion and pure muscular strength, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Messenger</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is the courier who endures great danger to deliver precious information; and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Ship\u2019s Wheel</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> perseveres in the face of hardship.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Auspicious Abilities: Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival, Thrown.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resplendencies</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crews overseen by </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Captain</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> gain +1 to Ability rolls for </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The House of Journeys\u2019 </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Auspicious Abilities.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Gull</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> appears to any superior or peer as if trustworthy for small tasks and hardworking despite any blatant slacking</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Mast</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> can find a job within hours of searching any populated area, insuring they are fed, clothed and sheltered.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Messenger</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> and their mount suffer no fatigue while they have a message or parcel to deliver. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Ship\u2019s Wheel</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> halves penalties from fatigue, injury and environmental conditions while set to a task they have sworn themselves to. </span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The House of Serenity</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Ewer</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is romantic pursuits based in affection and love of dreams; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Lovers </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">are physical lust, carnal indulgence and uneven relationships; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Musician</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> embodies contentment in the act of living; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Peacock</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> governs practical alliance, thoughtful breeding and considered partnerships; and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Matriarch </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">represents partnership tested and found stable.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Auspicious Abilities: Craft, Dodge, Linguistics, Performance, Socialize.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resplendencies</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Ewer</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> pays no willpower and ignores the bonus to resolve to overturn the Social influence of someone who shares an intimacy of love, affection or companionship with them.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Targets gain no bonus to Resolve against social influence made with Gestures and Body Language from </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Lovers</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Audiences of </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Musician</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> suffer -1 Resolve to resist indulgence, to relax or to open up to new people.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Peacock</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is never considered improperly dressed for any occasion.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those comforted by </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Matriarch </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">awaken resolved, recovering two willpower instead of one.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The House of Battles</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Banner</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> deals with reputation, story and awe; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Gauntlet</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is the choice between bad and worse; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Quiver</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is flexibility and fleetness of thought; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Shield</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is the ecstatic warrior who seeks battle without regard for victory; and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Spear</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is skill and discipline in armed conflict.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Auspicious Abilities: Archery, Athletics, Melee, Presence, War.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resplendencies</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those who have worked with or have heard and embrace the stories of </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Banner</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> are drawn to serve the cause.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Gauntlet</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> shows the character as someone capable of performing terrible actions which inspire the worst the imagination can bare and are always credible enough to attempt a Threaten action.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Quiver</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> can communicate simple ideas with just a glance to those they mutually share a Major or Defining Intimacy.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Shield</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is always treated as if wearing at least Light armor, even if standing in the nude.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Units lead by </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Spear</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> use their Willpower (if higher) for Rout Checks rather than the Willpower of the average fighter in the unit.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The House of Secrets</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Guardians</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> personify practical knowledge and rewards earned through long labor; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Key </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">represents wisdom discovered through scholarly study and intellectual understanding; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Mask</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is secret wisdom and things known but concealed; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Sorcerer </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">is the Exalt, god, geomancer and talisman maker; and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Treasure Trove</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is revealed wisdom, and knowledge or understanding held like a beacon. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Auspicious Abilities: Investigation, Larceny, Lore, Occult, Stealth</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resplendencies</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While standing vigilant, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Guardian</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> can sense when someone they are interacting with intends to take advantage of them.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Key</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> may declare that the Calibration gate should be present right at that moment in their current location, and so it is. There may be a slight delay if the gate is elsewhere. This always brings three paradox to </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Key</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Mask</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> cannot be clearly seen or overheard by magic, obscuring any attempt to spy through unconventional means.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Sorcerer</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> may bless some personal possession or random object (no more than once per scene) to be a minor talisman of their choosing to be given away. They may not keep it for themselves.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Treasure Trove</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is always treated as if cultured and educated and many turn to them to resolve disputes or solve difficult problems.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The House of Endings</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Corpse</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is the end of continuance; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Crow</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is the end of illusions and dreams; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Haywain</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is endings that cannot be easily described and gradual decline; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Rising Smoke</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is the end of journeys and paths, literal and metaphorical; and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Sword</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> brings the end of hope.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Auspicious Abilities: Awareness, Brawl, Bureaucracy, Integrity, Martial Arts, Medicine</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resplendencies</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Corpse</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> may bless a human soul (alive or a willing ghost) to pass into lethe upon their death (or immediately if dead already) to be reincarnated into a child born shortly after somewhere in Creation. This blessing brings three paradox to </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Corpse</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Crow</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> may, over the course of a few seconds or a full turn, make the Superior Sign of the Crow and become a raven, crow or other corvid. Their strength is reduced to 1 but their other traits remain uneffected. Their equipment and gear pass Elsewhere and are restored with their form.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Standing in the heart of a business or the floors of its shop, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Haywain</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> can instantly tell whether the business (and not a particular individual) is \u201cwholly corrupt\u201d, \u201cmostly corrupt\u201d, \u201csomewhat corrupt\u201d, \u201cmostly honest\u201d or \u201ctotally honest.\u201d </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Rising Smoke</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> can, once per day, burn a written note and have it appear one day later in a (sometimes highly implausible) location only it\u2019s recipient will find.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weight of </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Sword</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2019s destiny hangs on them in a way that everyone can feel. The meek will avoid their gaze, the troublemakers are contrite and the martially inclined are drawn to test their mettle.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crafting Destinies</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No other exalt has a mastery over the fates of the world like the sidereal exalted. With skillful hands they weave the destinies of others or themselves for powerful, strange effects. The Sidereal, from anywhere, can scribe a fate into destiny\u2019s design through a number of complex and ritual prayers to the pattern spiders that run the loom of fate. A Vizeer standing within loom of fate itself can craft a fate into being directly.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In order to create such a destiny, the Sidereal performs a day long ritual (requiring at least 8 hours of work) during which their words and desires bend fate and destiny into the desired shape. Each destiny must take a narrative shape, a goal that the Sidereal wishes to be and any number of conditions, details and events that will see that happen; the fate that results follows not only the word but the spirit of the destiny laid out. Additionally, they must pick an astral college with a domain that appropriately encompasses the destiny they wish create. At the end of this period, they roll (Charisma + [Performance or Craft(fate)] + [Relevant College]). The Difficulty of this roll is set as follows:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If shaping the fate of mortals, the difficulty is 3 plus the size of a battle group needed to encompass that many people. The mortals must be linked in some thematic sense, be it by location, bloodline, confluence of events or other related tie.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If shaping the fate of an Essence-user, the difficulty is equal to their Essence Score plus 3. Essence Users must be targeted individually and must reside within fate. This is the difficulty a Sidereal uses to enact fate upon themselves, including Resplendent Destinies. Only the sidereal may craft a fate for themselves or any of their resplendent destinies and the Essence score of their Resplendent Destinies is treated as 0 for this score.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If shaping the fate of the land, the difficulty is 2 for an area a square mile or less, plus 3 for every factor of ten larger (Difficulty 5 for 10 square miles, 8 for 100, etc).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add +1 to the Difficulty for a destiny that lasts no more than a year.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add +2 to the Difficulty for a destiny that lasts no more than a decade. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add +3 to the Difficulty for a destiny that lasts no more than a lifetime (A human lifetime).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add +4 to the Difficulty for a destiny that lasts unto the generations.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A day spent detailing the plans before hand reduces the difficulty by 1. A week spent drawing up horoscopes (requiring only a couple hours observing each night\u2019s sky) reduces this instead by 2.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failing this roll upsets the Pattern Spiders and gives the Sidereal 2 Paradox. Botching this roll instead gives 5. If successful, the Sidereal is empowered to enact the fate, which they must do in person. This fate is delivered by touching the recipient, a representative or leader of a group or standing in the heart of the land. A person or piece of land may only be subject to one crafted destiny at a time, and any new one will unravel existing ones.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While under a Crafted Destiny, a subject gains a number of blessings and curses:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any action they make that aligns with the narrative of the destiny is made at -1 Difficulty, or only fails on a Botch if the task is made at Difficulty 1. In contested rolls, they benefit from a Target Number of 6, or gain +1 to any static defenses.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any action they make that runs contrary to the narrative of the destiny is made at +1 Difficulty. In contested rolls, they roll at Target Number 8, and suffer -1 to static defenses.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lands subject to this Destiny take shape in much slower, more subtle means, typically affecting the plant and small animal life, diseases, minor geographical terrains and weather patterns.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resplendent Destinies</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Resplendent Destiny is a role a Sidereal assumes, hand crafted and complete. These destinies use the Loom of create a shallow, but powerful false identity, strong enough to withstand their Arcane Fate. Each of a Sidereal\u2019s destinies carry with them an identity, which conforms to one of the constellations represented by its college. As long as the destiny exists, the identity remains consistent and can be slipped into at a moment\u2019s notice, costing the Sidereal only 1 WP to don (there is no cost to dismiss).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Resplendent Destiny is created like any other Crafted Destiny, save that the narrative describes their life and how others perceive them; they must pick one constellation to represent the destiny. They may only have a number of destinies in a college equal to their dots in that college, and, as they fade from duration or are replaced by others, the memories of that destiny begin to fade from those that interacted with them (subject to Arcane Fate). Once a destiny fades, it can never be assumed or re-created again.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While wearing a Resplendent Destiny, the Sidereal gains the benefit of a unique power related to the constellation of that Destiny, which they may utilize at their discretion; see Resplendencies above in Astral Colleges for the effects. Additionally, each Resplendent Destiny may carry its own crafted destiny as well. This crafted destiny is only in effect when wearing the Resplendent Destiny, and while wearing it they are not subject to any other Crafted Destiny.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sidereal receives +3 non-charm dice on any rolls to convince others of the validity of this identity, even if it seems grossly inappropriate for their appearance, mannerisms or biology. Those they interact with suffer a -3 penalty to disbelieve the identity, or a -2 to static defenses where appropriate. The only exceptions to this are other sidereals, who cannot perceive a Resplendent Destiny at all.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}